  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lumen Technologies Government Solutions obligated $93.7M in FY2027 to date across 23 awards, with an average award size of $4.1M. Obligations are down 73.6% year over year. Lumen Technologies Government Solutions saw concentration in buyers: the Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for $93.4M of FY2027 obligations, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration accounted for $242K. Historical obligations show swings before FY2027: FY22 recorded $160M, FY23 recorded $352M, FY24 recorded $280M, FY25 recorded $423M, and FY26 recorded $355M. Lumen Technologies Government Solutions current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date, and the figures reported here are contract obligations except where tables list total contract values. The available FY2027 obligations indicate a much smaller current-year volume compared with the most recent full fiscal years, and a clear buyer concentration in the Department of Veterans Affairs. This snapshot can help contractors and analysts gauge buyer dependence and award-size norms for Lumen Technologies Government Solutions in the current fiscal period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did FY2027 obligations fall compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Lumen Technologies Government Solutions obligations fell 73.6% year over year. Lumen Technologies Government Solutions FY2027 to date obligations of $93.7M are much smaller than recent full-year totals, including FY26 at $355M and FY25 at $423M. Lumen Technologies Government Solutions FY2027 obligations are heavily concentrated with the Department of Veterans Affairs at $93.4M, which suggests buyer concentration in the current fiscal period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer, obligating $93.4M. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the next buyer, obligating $242K, followed by the Railroad Retirement Board at $5.8K. Several agencies show $0 in FY2027 to date obligations, including the Department of Agriculture and the Department of the Interior."
      }
    ]
  },
